description: Enforce one safe Terraform deployment path for every cloud capability
alwaysApply: true
---

# Terraform Cloud Deployment

When work creates or changes cloud infrastructure:

- Use Terraform as the only infrastructure owner. Do not mix SAM, CloudFormation, console steps, or application scripts into the same deployment path.
- Provide one documented root module per customer deployment path and use focused reusable leaf modules.
- Use encrypted remote state with locking, versioning, restricted access, and a documented bootstrap process.
- Make planning the default. Apply only an explicit reviewed saved plan.
- Never silently replace customer-owned resources or policies. Import, reference, or require explicit ownership.
- Deploy immutable application artifacts such as digest-pinned images.
- Use least privilege, encryption, private networking where supported, validated inputs, and useful non-secret outputs.
- Automate required bootstrap dependencies without creating a second deployment path.
- Keep code, examples, deployment instructions, rollback steps, and tests synchronized.
- Require CI to run `terraform fmt -check -recursive`, `terraform init -backend=false`, `terraform validate`, Terraform tests, and the repository-pinned security scanner.
- Put narrow scanner exceptions beside the affected resource with the check ID and a truthful reason. Do not use broad global skips to make CI pass.
- Report whether live cloud deployment was tested; never imply local validation proves a real deployment.
